<h2 id="whatsapp-automation-workflows-for-shopify-stores-worth-building"><b>WhatsApp Automation Workflows for Shopify Stores Worth Building </b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Below are the essential workflows every Shopify store should implement: </span></p>
<h3 id="1-welcome-journey"><b>1. Welcome Journey</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The welcome message is the first automated conversation your customer receives from your online store. When someone places a first order or opts in via </span><a href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">click-to-WhatsApp ads</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">, an automated welcome message creates a strong first impression and sets the stage for future engagement.</span></p>
<p><b>Trigger:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> First order placed, or WhatsApp opt-in through signup.</span></p>
<p><b>Workflow:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Customer Subscribes → Welcome Message → Brand Introduction → First-Purchase Offer</span></p>
<p><b>Template Example:</b> <i><span style="font-weight: 400;">“Thank you for shopping with [Brand Name]. We hope you love our product. Here’s an exclusive 25% off on your next order. Use code: [Code].”</span></i></p>
<h3 id="2-abandoned-cart-recovery"><b>2. Abandoned Cart Recovery</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">It is the highest-ROI automation for most stores. A customer adds items to the cart and leaves without checking out, which may be due to unexpected extra cost, or they’re comparing prices. A WhatsApp reminder with small incentives helps catch them while the interest is still fresh.</span></p>
<p><b>Trigger:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Checkout started, then left incomplete.</span></p>
<p><b>Workflow:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> cart abandoned → wait 30–60 minutes → send a reminder → send one follow-up → stop automatically once they buy.</span></p>
<p><b>Template Example: </b><i><span style="font-weight: 400;">“Hey [Customer Name], you left [Product name] in your cart. Grab it now before they get sold out. [Checkout link].”</span></i></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Stick to one or two reminders. Too many of them can feel pushy. Wanna know more? Check out our guide on </span><a href="/resources/blog/whatsapp-abandoned-cart-recovery/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">WhatsApp abandoned cart recovery</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></p>
<h3 id="3-cod-order-confirmation"><b>3. COD Order Confirmation</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Cash on delivery (COD) is still a popular payment option for Shopify stores. But it can also lead to fake orders, cancelled deliveries, and higher return-to-origin (RTO) costs. A simple confirmation message at the right time can fix that.</span></p>
<p><b>Trigger:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> A COD order is placed.</span></p>
<p><b>Workflow</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">: COD Order Placed → WhatsApp Confirmation Sent → Customer Confirms → Order Shipped</span></p>
<p><b>Template Example</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">:</span><i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> “Hi [Customer Name], your COD order #[Order Number] from [Brand Name] is ready to dispatch. Please confirm your order so we can dispatch it today. CTA: [Confirm Order] [Cancel Order].” </span></i></p>
<h3 id="4-order-and-shipping-updates"><b>4. Order and Shipping Updates</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Once a customer places an order, they want to know where their order is. WhatsApp automation helps an online store send real-time delivery updates automatically to keep customers informed at every stage.</span></p>
<p><b>Trigger:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Order status changes (confirmed, packed, shipped, out for delivery, delivered).</span></p>
<p><b>Workflow: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Order Confirmed → Order Packed → Order Shipped → Out for Delivery → Delivered</span></p>
<h3 id="5-post-purchase-follow-up"><b>5. Post-Purchase Follow-Up</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The sale is not a finish line. In fact, post-purchase is a great opportunity for a Shopify store to build loyalty and drive repetitive purchases. </span><a href="/resources/blog/whatsapp-automated-messages/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Send automated WhatsApp messages</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> for a thank-you note, review request, or personalized product recommendations.</span></p>
<p><b>Trigger:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Order marked as delivered.</span></p>
<p><b>Workflow:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Order Delivered → Thank-You Message → Review Request → Product Recommendation</span></p>
<p><b>Template Example:</b><i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> “Hey {Customer Name}, we hope you love our [Product name]. We love to hear your experience. It will help us improve. Share your review here [Review Link].” </span></i></p>
<h3 id="6-win-back-campaigns"><b>6. Win-Back Campaigns</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Not every customer comes back on their own. Running an automated win-back campaign helps re-engage these customers and bring them back to your store. It’s one piece of a bigger <a href="/resources/blog/whatsapp-remarketing/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WhatsApp remarketing strategy</a></span><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></p>
<p><b>Trigger:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> No purchase in 30, 60, or 90+ days.</span></p>
<p><b>Workflow:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> No Purchase for 30+ Days → Personalized Offer → Return Purchase</span></p>
<p><b>Template Message:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> “Hi John, we missed you. Did you miss us? Here’s your exclusive 15% off discount on your next purchase. Use the GET15 promo code.”</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">You can send loyalty rewards, exclusive offers, and personalized product recommendations to increase repeat sales and customer retention. </span></p>
<h3 id="7-back-in-stock-alerts"><b>7. Back-in-Stock Alerts</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Out-of-stock products can lead to missed sales. Using WhatsApp automation, Shopify stores can notify interested buyers the moment a product is back in stock. It helps increase conversion and recover lost leads.</span></p>
<p><b>Trigger:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> A product customers opted into comes back in stock.</span></p>
<p><b>Workflow:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Product Out of Stock → Customer Subscribes → Product Restocked → WhatsApp Alert Sent</span></p>
<p><b>Template Example:</b><i><span style="font-weight: 400;"> “Hey Sam, Good news! Your favourite [Product name] is back in stock. You’ve been eyeing it for a long time. Buy it now before it gets sold out again. Shop now: [Product link].” </span></i></p>
<h2 id="how-to-set-up-whatsapp-marketing-automation-on-shopify-step-by-step"><b>How to Set Up WhatsApp Marketing Automation on Shopify (Step-by-Step)</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Setting up WhatsApp marketing automation for Shopify is a simple process. Below are the steps to follow:</span></p>
<p><b>Step 1: Get access to a WhatsApp Business AP:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Connect with an official WhatsApp API provider like HelloBotz to access the API. This gets you:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">A verified Meta Business Manager account</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">A dedicated WhatsApp number, never used on the regular app</span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">A verified business profile</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Here’s </span><a href="/resources/blog/apply-for-whatsapp-business-api/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">how to apply for WhatsApp Business API</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. </span></p>
<p><b>Step 2: Connect the App to Your Shopify Store: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Go to the </span><a href="https://apps.shopify.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Shopify App Store</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> and install the </span><a href="https://apps.shopify.com/HelloBotz-whatsapp-chatbot-api/reviews" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">HelloBotz Shopify app</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. It will automatically sync your products, customer details, and order data to trigger automated messages.</span></p>
<p><b>Step 3: Collect Customer Opt-ins</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">: Before sending marketing messages, ensure your customers have agreed to hear from your brand. Collect customer opt-ins via an opt-in checkbox or by </span><a href="/resources/blog/embed-whatsapp-chat-on-shopify/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">embedding a WhatsApp chat widget on your Shopify</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> website.</span></p>
<p><b>Step 4: Create Your Message Templates: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Go to the template section in your app dashboard. Select a pre-approved template for a specific event like order confirmation, shipping updates, cart reminder, or more. </span><a href="/resources/blog/how-to-create-or-apply-new-whatsapp-business-api-message-templates-using-HelloBotz/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Create and submit a WhatsApp template</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> for Meta approval if the app doesn’t include default templates.</span></p>
<p><b>Step 5: Map Triggers:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> It’s time to map approved templates to their corresponding Shopify event. For example, map the cart recovery template to the abandoned checkout event. You can set up your preferred time delay for automated sequences.</span></p>
<p><b>Step 6: Test &amp; Go Live:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Do a small test on your own personal phone number first to make sure that the automation triggers correctly before going live.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Once you set up everything, your whole system will run on autopilot without anyone in your team lifting a finger. </span></p>
