<h2 id="common-mistakes-to-avoid-with-shopify-whatsapp-automation"><b>Common Mistakes to Avoid with Shopify WhatsApp Automation </b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">WhatsApp marketing automation for Shopify can help boost sales and improve customer engagement when used correctly. Here are some common mistakes you should avoid:</span></p>
<ol>
<li><b>Skipping Customer Opt-Ins</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">: Always collect customer opt-ins to send promotional messages on WhatsApp. Ignoring this can get your number reported as spam and lower your message quality rating.</span></li>
<li><b>Treating every customer the same: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Not all customers have the same interests or buying behaviour. Segment your contact list based on past purchases, interest, and activity to send relevant messages and boost engagement.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-weight: 400;">3</span><b>. Failing to Provide a Human Handoff:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Automation works great, but some queries require a real person to talk. Always offer an easy way to connect with a human agent when needed.</span></li>
